------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY CHECKLIST
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  States reproduced (every branch the web source renders; no hidden surfaces):
    - loading  -> TSSkeleton (web <Skeleton h-48>)
    - empty    -> ContentUnavailableView (web EmptyState "Send a request...")
    - loaded   -> FadeIn { status bar (success<300 / warning<400 / danger tone) +
                  monospaced body + collapsible Response Headers }
    - history strip (hidden when empty, web `if length===0 return null`)
    Note: the web leaf has no separate fetch-error / stale / offline chrome — it
    only ever receives a finished `response` (or null); an errored request
    surfaces as the danger-toned status response. Documented in Model header
    (matches the 0009 TelemetryErrorsPanel precedent's same finding).
  i18n keys (every web t() key resolves through P1/S10 facade, no literals):
    playground.response, playground.noResponse, playground.responseHeaders,
    playground.history, playground.codeSnippet, playground.copy
    (+ native chrome: responseViewer.loadingA11y/.copied/.replayHint)
  Accessibility: status bar + history chips carry VoiceOver labels; disclosure +
    format-tab + copy controls labelled with isButton/isSelected traits;
    Dynamic Type via system fonts; Reduce Motion via TSSkeleton/TSFadeIn.
  Telemetry: ResponseViewerModel.start() emits view.opened(surface:"ResponseViewer")
    exactly once (P1/S11 diagnostics contract).
  Charts/maps: none (web source uses neither) — no Swift Charts / MapKit needed.

